-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 17 (Offences against property), part 3:
--   Cheating                                        ss 415-420A
--   Fraudulent deeds and dispositions of property   ss 421-424B
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (inputs/PC1871.txt). Section text copied mechanically.
--
-- Before reading:
--
-- * `Cheating Facts` serves ss 415-420 and keeps the reference row's field
--   names (reference/drafts-row/cheating-415-417-420.l4), so the catalogue's
--   leaves for ss 417 and 420 are unchanged; it adds the leaves of ss 416
--   (personation), 416B (remote communication) and 418. The reference row's
--   `by remote communication` leaf is replaced by s 416B's own words
--   (fork P-4).
-- * s 420 punishes differently in (1) and (2), with different elements, so it
--   has `offence under s 420(1)` and `offence under s 420(2)` (notes/PLAN.md
--   §2); the reference row's single `offence under s 420` is not kept (fork P-4).
-- * ss 416A, 420A, 421-424 and 424A-424B are families of their own.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`

§ `Chapter 17 - Offences against property: cheating`

§§ `The facts of one deception`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 415-420 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC ss 124 and 125 require
DECLARE `Cheating Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim                IS A STRING  @desc The name of the person deceived, as it is to appear in the charge - for example "Wong Fei Hsia"
    `victim described as` IS A STRING  @desc How the charge describes the person deceived, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `victim pronoun`      IS A Pronoun @desc The pronoun the charge uses for the person deceived

    -- s 415 "by deceiving any person"
    `deceived the victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused deceive the victim? A dishonest concealment of facts is a deception (Explanation 1); a representation through an agent counts (Explanation 3); a company can be deceived though no officer is (Explanation 4, illustration (k)).
    `the deception`       IS A STRING  @desc What the victim was deceived into, as it is to read after "by deceiving him/her" - for example "to believe that the price of a pencil casing is worth $5.25"

    -- "fraudulently or dishonestly" (s 25, s 24)
    fraudulently          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act fraudulently (s 25)? Mere breach of contract is not of itself proof of an original fraudulent intent (Explanation 2, illustration (g)).
    dishonestly           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act dishonestly (s 24)?

    -- first limb
    deliver               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim induced to deliver property to anyone?
    `cause the delivery`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim induced to cause the delivery of property to anyone?
    `consent that any person shall retain any property`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim induced to consent that anyone keep property?
    `the property`        IS A STRING  @desc What was delivered or retained, as it is to read after "to deliver to you" - for example "the said item for only $5.25"

    -- second limb
    intentionally         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to induce the victim to act, or to refrain, as they did? (fault element, s 26C)
    `do`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim induced to do something they would not have done but for the deception?
    `omit to do`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim induced to leave undone something they would otherwise have done?
    `the act or omission` IS A STRING  @desc What the victim did or left undone, as it is to read after "to"
    causes                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that act or omission cause damage or harm?
    `likely to cause`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that act or omission likely to cause damage or harm?
    damage                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Damage to any person?
    harm                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Harm to any person?
    body                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... in body?
    mind                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... in mind?
    reputation            IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... in reputation?
    property              IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... in property?

    -- s 416
    `pretending to be some other person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cheat by pretending to be some other person, real or imaginary (Explanation)?
    `knowingly substituting one person for another`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cheat by knowingly substituting one person for another?
    `representing that he or any other person is a person other than he or such other person really is`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cheat by representing that he, or someone else, is a person other than who he or they really are?

    -- s 416B
    `the deception is conducted mainly by way of remote communication with the person deceived`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the deception conducted mainly by remote communication with the person deceived - through the Internet, telephone or other communication device, television or radio, or any other technology for facilitating communication (s 416B(2))?
    `a system or method the Minister has declared is not remote communication`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that communication through a specific system or method that the Minister, by order in the Gazette, has declared not to be remote communication (s 416B(2))?

    -- s 418
    `with the knowledge that he is likely thereby to cause wrongful loss to a person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cheat knowing that he was likely thereby to cause wrongful loss (s 23) to a person? (s 418)
    `whose interest, in the transaction to which the cheating relates, he was bound either by law or by a legal contract to protect`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that a person whose interest in the transaction the accused was bound, by law or by a legal contract, to protect? (s 418)

    -- s 420(1): the alternative to delivery
    `make, alter or destroy a valuable security`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim induced to make, alter or destroy the whole or any part of a valuable security (s 30), or anything signed or sealed that is capable of being converted into one?

§§ `s 415 - cheating`

-- 415. Whoever, by deceiving any person, whether or not such deception was the sole
-- or main inducement, fraudulently or dishonestly induces the person so deceived to
-- deliver or cause the delivery of any property to any person, or to consent that any person
-- shall retain any property, or intentionally induces the person so deceived to do or omit to
-- do anything which he would not do or omit to do if he were not so deceived, and which
-- act or omission causes or is likely to cause damage or harm to any person in body, mind,
-- reputation or property, is said to "cheat".
--
-- Explanation 1.-A dishonest concealment of facts is a deception within the meaning of this section.
--
-- Explanation 2.-Mere breach of contract is not of itself proof of an original fraudulent intent.
--
-- Explanation 3.-Whoever makes a representation through any agent is to be treated as having made
-- the representation himself.
--
-- Explanation 4.-A person that is a company or association or body of persons, whether incorporated
-- or not, can be deceived for the purposes of this section, even though none of its individual officers,
-- employees or agents is personally deceived.
--
-- Explanation 5.-A person that is a company or association or body of persons, whether incorporated
-- or not, can be induced to act in a manner mentioned in this section even though none of its individual
-- officers, employees or agents is personally induced to act in such manner.
--
-- Illustrations
--
-- (a) A, by falsely pretending to be in the Government service, intentionally deceives Z, and thus
-- dishonestly induces Z to let him have on credit goods for which he does not mean to pay. A cheats.
--
-- (b) A, by putting a counterfeit mark on an article, intentionally deceives Z into a belief that this
-- article was made by a certain celebrated manufacturer, and thus dishonestly induces Z to buy and pay
-- for the article. A cheats.
--
-- (c) A, by exhibiting to Z a false sample of an article, intentionally deceives Z into believing that the
-- article corresponds with the sample, and thereby dishonestly induces Z to buy and pay for the article. A
-- cheats.
--
-- (d) A, by tendering in payment for an article a bill on a house with which A keeps no money, and by
-- which A expects that the bill will be dishonoured, intentionally deceives Z, and thereby dishonestly
-- induces Z to deliver the article, intending not to pay for it. A cheats.
--
-- (e) A, by pledging as diamonds articles which he knows are not diamonds, intentionally deceives Z,
-- and thereby dishonestly induces Z to lend money. A cheats.
--
-- (f) A intentionally deceives Z into a belief that A means to repay any money that Z may lend to him,
--
-- and thereby dishonestly induces Z to lend him money, A not intending to repay it. A cheats.
--
-- (g) A intentionally deceives Z into a belief that A means to deliver to Z a certain quantity of pepper
-- which he does not intend to deliver, and thereby dishonestly induces Z to advance money upon the faith
-- of such delivery. A cheats; but if A, at the time of obtaining the money, intends to deliver the pepper,
-- and afterwards breaks his contract and does not deliver it, he does not cheat, but is liable only to a civil
-- action for breach of contract.
--
-- (h) A intentionally deceives Z into a belief that A has performed A's part of a contract made with Z,
-- which he has not performed, and thereby dishonestly induces Z to pay money. A cheats.
--
-- (i) A sells and conveys an estate to B. A, knowing that in consequence of such sale he has no right to
-- the property, sells or mortgages the same to Z without disclosing the fact of the previous sale and
-- conveyance to B, and receives the purchase or mortgage money from Z. A cheats.
--
-- (j) A, playing with false dice, or marked cards, wins money from B. A cheats.
--
-- (k) A places an order for concert tickets in the automated concert ticketing system of a company, Z,
-- using stolen credit card details, and thereby causes Z's ticketing system to electronically deliver the
-- electronic concert tickets to A. Z has been deceived and induced into delivering the tickets to A even
-- though no human officer, employee or agent of Z has been personally deceived or induced.
--
-- [15/2019]
@export Whether the accused "cheats" within section 415 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The deception, and what it induced the person deceived to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE cheats f IF
        "Whoever, by"
   ...  f's `deceived the victim`
   ...  ", whether or not such deception was the sole or main inducement,"
   ...  (    (    (    f's fraudulently
                  OR   f's dishonestly )
             AND  "induces the person so deceived to"
             AND  (    f's deliver
                  OR   f's `cause the delivery`
                  OR   f's `consent that any person shall retain any property` ) )
        OR   (    f's intentionally
             AND  "induces the person so deceived to"
             AND  (    f's `do`
                  OR   f's `omit to do` )
             AND  "anything which he would not do or omit to do if he were not so deceived, and which act or omission"
             AND  (    f's causes
                  OR   f's `likely to cause` )
             AND  (    f's damage
                  OR   f's harm )
             AND  "to any person in"
             AND  (    f's body
                  OR   f's mind
                  OR   f's reputation
                  OR   f's property ) ) )
   ...  ", is said to cheat"

§§ `s 416 - cheating by personation`

-- 416. A person is said to "cheat by personation", if he cheats by pretending to be some
--
-- other person, or by knowingly substituting one person for another, or representing that he
-- or any other person is a person other than he or such other person really is.
--
-- Explanation.-The offence is committed whether the individual personated is a real or an imaginary
-- person.
--
-- Illustrations
--
-- (a) A cheats by pretending to be a certain rich banker of the same name. A cheats by personation.
--
-- (b) A cheats by pretending to be B, a person who is deceased. A cheats by personation.
@export Whether the accused "cheats by personation" within section 416 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The cheating, and how the accused represented who anyone was
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cheats by personation` f IF
        "A person is said to cheat by personation, if he"
   ...  cheats f
   ...  "by"
   ...  (    f's `pretending to be some other person`
        OR   f's `knowingly substituting one person for another`
        OR   f's `representing that he or any other person is a person other than he or such other person really is` )

§§ `s 416A - illegally obtained personal information`

-- 416A.-(1) A person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who, knowing or having reason
-- to believe that any personal information about another person (B) (being an individual)
-- was obtained without B's consent -
--
-- (a) obtains or retains the personal information; or
--
-- (b) supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available, by any means, the
-- personal information.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (2) It is not an offence under subsection (1)(a) if the person obtained or retained the
-- personal information for a purpose other than -
--
-- (a) for use in committing, or in facilitating the commission of, any offence
-- under this Code or any other written law; or
--
-- (b) for supply, transmission or making available by any means for the personal
-- information to be used in committing, or in facilitating the commission of,
-- any offence under this Code or any other written law.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (3) It is not an offence under subsection (1)(b) if -
--
-- (a) the person did the act for a purpose other than for the personal information
-- to be used in committing, or in facilitating the commission of, any offence
-- under this Code or any other written law; and
--
-- (b) the person did not know or have reason to believe that the personal
-- information will be or is likely to be used to commit, or facilitate the
-- commission of, any offence under this Code or any other written law.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (4) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b), a person does not transmit or make
-- available personal information merely because the person provides, or operates facilities
-- for network access, or provides services relating to, or provides connections for, the
-- transmission or routing of data.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (5) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be
-- punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine which
-- may extend to $10,000, or with both.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (6) For the purpose of proving under subsection (1) that a person knows or has reason
-- to believe that any personal information of an individual (B) was obtained without B's
-- consent, it is not necessary for the prosecution to prove the particulars of the obtaining of
-- the personal information, such as who obtained the information and when it took place.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (7) In this section -
--
-- (a) personal information is any information, whether true or not, about an
-- individual of a type that is commonly used alone or in combination with
-- other information to identify or purport to identify an individual, including
--
-- (but not limited to) biometric data, name, address, date of birth, national
-- registration identity card number, passport number, a written, electronic or
-- digital signature, user authentication code, credit card or debit card
-- number, and password; and
--
-- (b) a reference to an offence under this Code includes an offence under
-- subsection (1).
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 416A
`punishment prescribed by s 416A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "416A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine which may extend to $10,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 416A - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `Personal Information Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the personal information`
                          IS A STRING  @desc The personal information, as it is to read in the charge - for example "the NRIC number and credit card number of one Tan Ah Kow"
    `personal information about another person, being an individual`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it personal information - any information, true or not, about an individual, of a type commonly used alone or with other information to identify or purport to identify an individual (biometric data, name, address, date of birth, NRIC or passport number, signature, user authentication code, card number, password) (s 416A(7)(a))?
    `knowing or having reason to believe that it was obtained without that person's consent`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know or have reason to believe that it was obtained without the individual's consent? The prosecution need not prove who obtained it or when (s 416A(6)).
    `obtains or retains the personal information`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obtain or retain it? (s 416A(1)(a))
    `supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available the personal information`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused supply, offer to supply, transmit or make it available, by any means? Merely providing or operating network access or data routing is not transmitting or making available (s 416A(4)). (s 416A(1)(b))
    `for use in committing, or facilitating, any offence`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obtain, retain or pass it on for it to be used in committing, or facilitating, any offence under the Code (including s 416A) or any other written law - or, under (1)(a), for supply for such use? (s 416A(2), (3)(a))
    `knew or had reason to believe it will or is likely to be used to commit or facilitate an offence`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know or have reason to believe that it will be, or is likely to be, used to commit or facilitate any offence? (s 416A(3)(b))

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 416A of the Penal Code 1871 (illegally obtained personal information)
GIVEN f IS A `Personal Information Facts` @desc The information, and what the accused did with it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 416A` f IF
        "(1) A person (A) shall be guilty of an offence who,"
   ...  f's `knowing or having reason to believe that it was obtained without that person's consent`
   ...  "that any"
   ...  f's `personal information about another person, being an individual`
   ...  (    (    f's `obtains or retains the personal information`
             AND  "(2) It is not an offence under subsection (1)(a) if the person obtained or retained the personal information for a purpose other than"
             AND  f's `for use in committing, or facilitating, any offence` )
        OR   (    f's `supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available the personal information`
             AND  "(3) It is not an offence under subsection (1)(b) if (a) the purpose was other than such use, and (b) the person did not know or have reason to believe"
             AND  (    f's `for use in committing, or facilitating, any offence`
                  OR   f's `knew or had reason to believe it will or is likely to be used to commit or facilitate an offence` ) ) )

@export Frame a charge under section 416A of the Penal Code 1871 (illegally obtained personal information), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Personal Information Facts` @desc The information, what the accused did with it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 416A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "416A(1)" "illegally obtained personal information"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 416A`'s words)
        (`offence under s 416A` f)
        (CONCAT "knowing or having reason to believe that personal information, to wit, ", f's `the personal information`,
                ", was obtained without the consent of the individual it concerns, did ",
                (`joined with` ", and did " (concat (LIST
                    (`included if` (f's `obtains or retains the personal information`) "obtain or retain the said personal information"),
                    (`included if` (f's `supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available the personal information`) "supply, offer to supply, transmit or make available the said personal information")))))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `knowing or having reason to believe that it was obtained without that person's consent`) "knowing or having reason to believe that it was obtained without that person's consent"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `personal information about another person, being an individual`) "personal information about another person, being an individual (section 416A(7))"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `obtains or retains the personal information` OR f's `supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available the personal information`) "obtains or retains, or supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available, the personal information"),
            (`missing unless` (`offence under s 416A` f) "a purpose of use in, or knowledge of likely use in, committing or facilitating an offence (section 416A(2) and (3))")))

§§ `s 416B - cheating by remote communication`

-- 416B.-(1) A person (A) is said to "cheat by remote communication" if A cheats by
-- deceiving another person (Z), and the deception is conducted mainly by way of remote
-- communication with Z.
--
-- (2) In this section, "remote communication" means communication through -
--
-- (a) the Internet;
--
-- (b) telephone or any other communication device;
--
-- (c) television or radio; or
--
-- (d) any other kind of electronic or other technology for facilitating
-- communication,
--
-- but excludes any specific system or method of communication that the Minister, by order
-- in the Gazette, declares is not remote communication for the purposes of this section.
--
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 30/12/2025]
@export Whether the accused "cheats by remote communication" within section 416B of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The cheating, and how the deception was conducted
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cheats by remote communication` f IF
        "(1) A person (A) is said to cheat by remote communication if A"
   ...  cheats f
   ...  "by deceiving another person (Z), and"
   ...  f's `the deception is conducted mainly by way of remote communication with the person deceived`
   ...  "(2) ... but excludes"
   ...  NOT f's `a system or method the Minister has declared is not remote communication`

§§ `s 417 - punishment for cheating`

-- 417. Whoever cheats shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
-- extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 417
`punishment prescribed by s 417` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "417"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 417 of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating)
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The deception, and what it induced the person deceived to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 417` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  cheats f

§§ `s 418 - cheating with knowledge that wrongful loss may be thereby caused to a person whose interest the offender is bound to protect`

-- 418. Whoever cheats with the knowledge that he is likely thereby to cause wrongful
-- loss to a person whose interest, in the transaction to which the cheating relates, he was
-- bound either by law or by a legal contract to protect shall be punished with imprisonment
-- for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 418
`punishment prescribed by s 418` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "418"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 418 of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating with knowledge that wrongful loss may be caused to a person whose interest the offender is bound to protect)
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The cheating, and the accused's duty to the person who stood to lose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 418` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  cheats f
   ...  f's `with the knowledge that he is likely thereby to cause wrongful loss to a person`
   ...  f's `whose interest, in the transaction to which the cheating relates, he was bound either by law or by a legal contract to protect`

§§ `s 419 - punishment for cheating by personation`

-- 419. Whoever cheats by personation shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--
-- which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 419
`punishment prescribed by s 419` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "419"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 419 of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating by personation)
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The cheating, and the personation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 419` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `cheats by personation` f

§§ `s 420 - cheating and dishonestly inducing a delivery of property`

-- 420.-(1) Whoever cheats and thereby dishonestly induces the person deceived to
-- deliver or cause the delivery of any property to any person, or to make, alter or destroy
-- the whole or any part of a valuable security, or anything which is signed or sealed, and
-- which is capable of being converted into a valuable security, shall be punished with
-- imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or
-- to caning or to both.
--
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 30/12/2025]
--
-- (2) Whoever cheats by remote communication and thereby dishonestly induces any of
-- the acts mentioned in subsection (1) shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
-- which may extend to 10 years and with caning with not less than 6 strokes, and shall also
-- be liable to fine.
--
-- [15/2019]
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 30/12/2025]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 420(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 420(1)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "420(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning or to both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 420(2)
`punishment prescribed by s 420(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "420(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years and with caning with not less than 6 strokes, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall be punished with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS JUST 6
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 420(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating and dishonestly inducing a delivery of property)
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The deception, and what it induced the person deceived to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 420(1)` f IF
        "(1) Whoever"
   ...  cheats f
   ...  "and thereby"
   ...  f's dishonestly
   ...  "induces the person deceived to"
   ...  (    f's deliver
        OR   f's `cause the delivery`
        OR   f's `make, alter or destroy a valuable security` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 420(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating by remote communication and dishonestly inducing a delivery of property)
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The deception, how it was conducted, and what it induced
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 420(2)` f IF
        "(2) Whoever"
   ...  `cheats by remote communication` f
   ...  "and thereby"
   ...  f's dishonestly
   ...  "induces any of the acts mentioned in subsection (1)"
   ...  (    f's deliver
        OR   f's `cause the delivery`
        OR   f's `make, alter or destroy a valuable security` )

§§ `The cheating charges`

-- CPC s 125 illustration (b): "The charge must set out the manner in which A
-- cheated B." Read off the leaves that are TRUE, in the order of the section.
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`second limb` f MEANS
    f's intentionally AND (f's `do` OR f's `omit to do`)

GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the adverb` f MEANS
    `joined with` " and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's fraudulently) "fraudulently"),
        (`included if` (f's dishonestly) "dishonestly"),
        (`included if` (`second limb` f) "intentionally")))

GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`what the victim was induced to do` f MEANS
    `joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's deliver) ("deliver to you " APPEND f's `the property`)),
        (`included if` (f's `cause the delivery`) ("cause the delivery of " APPEND f's `the property`)),
        (`included if` (f's `consent that any person shall retain any property`) ("consent to the retention of " APPEND f's `the property`)),
        (`included if` (f's `make, alter or destroy a valuable security`) ("make, alter or destroy " APPEND f's `the property`)),
        (`included if` (`second limb` f) (f's `the act or omission`))))

GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the manner of the cheating` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did cheat ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)),
           " by deceiving ", (`object pronoun` (f's `victim pronoun`)), " ", f's `the deception`,
           ", and by such manner of deception, you ", (`the adverb` f), " induced the said ", f's victim,
           " to ", (`what the victim was induced to do` f),
           " which ", (`subject pronoun` (f's `victim pronoun`)), " would not have done, had ", (`subject pronoun` (f's `victim pronoun`)), " not been so deceived"

GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of cheating not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `deceived the victim`) "by deceiving any person"),
        (`missing unless` (f's fraudulently OR f's dishonestly OR f's intentionally) "fraudulently, dishonestly or intentionally"),
        (`missing unless` (f's deliver OR f's `cause the delivery` OR f's `consent that any person shall retain any property` OR `second limb` f) "induces the person so deceived to deliver or cause the delivery of property, to consent to its retention, or to do or omit to do anything"),
        (`missing unless` (cheats f) "the elements of section 415 taken together"))

GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`missing dishonest inducement of delivery` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's dishonestly) "dishonestly (section 420 requires dishonesty; fraud alone is section 417)"),
        (`missing unless` (f's deliver OR f's `cause the delivery` OR f's `make, alter or destroy a valuable security`) "induces the person deceived to deliver or cause the delivery of property, or to make, alter or destroy a valuable security"))

@export Frame a charge under section 417 of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The deception, what it induced, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 417` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "417" "cheating"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 417`'s words)
        (`offence under s 417` f)
        (`the manner of the cheating` f)
        (`elements of cheating not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 418 of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating with knowledge that wrongful loss may be caused to a person whose interest the offender is bound to protect), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The deception, the duty, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 418` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "418" "cheating with knowledge that wrongful loss may be thereby caused to a person whose interest the offender is bound to protect"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 418`'s words)
        (`offence under s 418` f)
        (CONCAT (`the manner of the cheating` f), ", with the knowledge that you were likely thereby to cause wrongful loss to the said ", f's victim,
                ", whose interest in the transaction you were bound by law or by a legal contract to protect")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of cheating not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `with the knowledge that he is likely thereby to cause wrongful loss to a person`) "with the knowledge that he is likely thereby to cause wrongful loss to a person"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `whose interest, in the transaction to which the cheating relates, he was bound either by law or by a legal contract to protect`) "whose interest, in the transaction to which the cheating relates, he was bound either by law or by a legal contract to protect")))

@export Frame a charge under section 419 of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating by personation), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The deception, the personation, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 419` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "419" "cheating by personation"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 419`'s words)
        (`offence under s 419` f)
        (CONCAT (`the manner of the cheating` f), ", and did thereby cheat by personation")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of cheating not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `pretending to be some other person` OR f's `knowingly substituting one person for another` OR f's `representing that he or any other person is a person other than he or such other person really is`) "by pretending to be some other person, or by knowingly substituting one person for another, or representing that he or any other person is a person other than he or such other person really is (section 416)")))

@export Frame a charge under section 420(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating and dishonestly inducing a delivery of property), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The deception, what it induced, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 420(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "420" "cheating and dishonestly inducing a delivery of property"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 420(1)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 420(1)` f)
        (`the manner of the cheating` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of cheating not made out` f), (`missing dishonest inducement of delivery` f)))

@export Frame a charge under section 420(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (cheating by remote communication and dishonestly inducing a delivery of property), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Cheating Facts` @desc The deception, how it was conducted, what it induced, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 420(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "420(2)" "cheating by remote communication and dishonestly inducing a delivery of property"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 420(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 420(2)` f)
        (CONCAT (`the manner of the cheating` f), ", the said deception being conducted mainly by way of remote communication with the said ", f's victim)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of cheating not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (`cheats by remote communication` f) "the deception is conducted mainly by way of remote communication (section 416B)"),
                      (`missing dishonest inducement of delivery` f)))

§§ `s 420A - obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently`

-- 420A.-(1) A person shall be guilty of an offence if he obtains services for himself or
-- another person dishonestly or fraudulently and -
--
-- (a) the services are made available on the basis that payment has been, is
-- being or will be made for or in respect of them;
--
-- (b) the person obtains the services without any payment having been made for
-- or in respect of them or without payment having been made in full; and
--
-- (c) when the person obtains the services -
-- (i) the person knows that they are being made available on the basis
-- mentioned in paragraph (a) or that they might be; and
--
-- (ii) the person intends that payment will not be made or will not be
-- made in full.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be
-- liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years, or to fine, or to both.
--
-- Explanation.-The services obtained are not excluded from this section merely because such
-- services also involve the provision of goods or other things.
--
-- Illustration
--
-- A obtains services in the form of air transportation on an airline from Singapore to an overseas
-- destination. A is also served food and beverages on the airline. A has obtained services even though A
-- has also been provided with food and beverages.
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 420A
`punishment prescribed by s 420A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "420A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years, or to fine, or to both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 420A - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `Services Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the services`        IS A STRING  @desc The services obtained, as it is to read in the charge - for example "air transportation from Singapore to Bangkok on Singapore Airlines flight SQ 978"
    `obtains services for himself or another person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obtain services for himself or another? Services are not excluded because they also involve goods or other things (Explanation, illustration).
    dishonestly           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act dishonestly (s 24)?
    fraudulently          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act fraudulently (s 25)?
    `made available on the basis that payment has been, is being or will be made`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Were the services made available on the basis that payment has been, is being or will be made for them?
    `without any payment having been made, or without payment having been made in full`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Did the accused obtain them without paying, or without paying in full?
    `knows that they are being made available on that basis, or that they might be`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c)(i) When obtaining them, did the accused know that they were, or might be, made available on that basis?
    `intends that payment will not be made, or will not be made in full`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c)(ii) When obtaining them, did the accused intend that payment would not be made, or not in full?

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 420A of the Penal Code 1871 (obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently)
GIVEN f IS A `Services Facts` @desc The services, and how they were obtained
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 420A` f IF
        "(1) A person shall be guilty of an offence if he"
   ...  f's `obtains services for himself or another person`
   ...  (    f's dishonestly
        OR   f's fraudulently )
   ...  "and - (a)"
   ...  f's `made available on the basis that payment has been, is being or will be made`
   ...  "(b)"
   ...  f's `without any payment having been made, or without payment having been made in full`
   ...  "(c) when the person obtains the services - (i)"
   ...  f's `knows that they are being made available on that basis, or that they might be`
   ...  "(ii)"
   ...  f's `intends that payment will not be made, or will not be made in full`

@export Frame a charge under section 420A of the Penal Code 1871 (obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Services Facts` @desc The services, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 420A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "420A(1)" "obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 420A`'s words)
        (`offence under s 420A` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (`joined with` " and " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's dishonestly) "dishonestly"), (`included if` (f's fraudulently) "fraudulently")))),
                " obtain services, to wit, ", f's `the services`,
                ", which were made available on the basis that payment would be made for them, without payment having been made in full, knowing that they were being made available on that basis and intending that payment would not be made in full")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `obtains services for himself or another person`) "obtains services for himself or another person"),
            (`missing unless` (f's dishonestly OR f's fraudulently) "dishonestly or fraudulently"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `made available on the basis that payment has been, is being or will be made`) "(a) the services are made available on the basis that payment has been, is being or will be made"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `without any payment having been made, or without payment having been made in full`) "(b) without payment, or without payment in full"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `knows that they are being made available on that basis, or that they might be`) "(c)(i) knows that they are being made available on that basis, or might be"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intends that payment will not be made, or will not be made in full`) "(c)(ii) intends that payment will not be made, or not in full")))

§ `Chapter 17 - Offences against property: fraudulent deeds and dispositions of property`

§§ `The facts of one disposition`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 421-424 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `Fraudulent Disposition Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the property`        IS A STRING  @desc The property, debt, deed or claim, as it is to read in the charge
    dishonestly           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act dishonestly (s 24)?
    fraudulently          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act fraudulently (s 25)?

    -- s 421
    `removes, conceals, or delivers to any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused remove, conceal, or deliver to any person, any property? (s 421)
    `transfers or causes to be transferred to any person, without adequate consideration`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused transfer, or cause to be transferred, any property to any person without adequate consideration? (s 421)
    `intending thereby to prevent, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby prevent, the distribution of that property according to law among his creditors or the creditors of any other person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend thereby to prevent, or know it likely that he would thereby prevent, the distribution of that property according to law among his creditors or another person's creditors? (s 421)

    -- s 422
    `prevents any debt or demand due to himself or to any other person from being made available according to law for payment of his debts or the debts of such other person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused prevent a debt or demand due to himself or another from being made available according to law for payment of his, or that other's, debts? (s 422)

    -- s 423
    `signs, executes, or becomes a party to any deed or instrument which purports to transfer or subject to any charge any property, or any interest therein`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused sign, execute, or become a party to a deed or instrument purporting to transfer, or to subject to a charge, any property or interest in property? (s 423)
    `which contains any false statement relating to the consideration for such transfer or charge, or relating to the person or persons for whose use or benefit it is really intended to operate`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that deed or instrument contain a false statement about the consideration, or about the person or persons for whose use or benefit it is really meant to operate? (s 423)

    -- s 424
    `conceals or removes any property of himself or any other person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused conceal or remove any property of his own or another's? (s 424)
    `assists in the concealment or removal thereof`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused assist in concealing or removing it? (s 424)
    `releases any demand or claim to which he is entitled`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused release a demand or claim to which he was entitled? (s 424 - this limb requires dishonesty; fraud alone is not enough)

GIVEN f IS A `Fraudulent Disposition Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`dishonestly or fraudulently, recited` f MEANS
    `joined with` " or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's dishonestly) "dishonestly"), (`included if` (f's fraudulently) "fraudulently")))

GIVEN f IS A `Fraudulent Disposition Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`missing dishonestly or fraudulently` f MEANS
    `missing unless` (f's dishonestly OR f's fraudulently) "dishonestly or fraudulently"

§§ `s 421 - dishonest or fraudulent removal or concealment of property to prevent distribution among creditors`

-- 421. Whoever dishonestly or fraudulently removes, conceals, or delivers to any
-- person, or transfers or causes to be transferred to any person, without adequate
-- consideration, any property, intending thereby to prevent, or knowing it to be likely that
-- he will thereby prevent, the distribution of that property according to law among his
-- creditors or the creditors of any other person, shall be punished with imprisonment for a
-- term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 421
`punishment prescribed by s 421` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "421"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 421 of the Penal Code 1871 (dishonest or fraudulent removal or concealment of property to prevent distribution among creditors)
GIVEN f IS A `Fraudulent Disposition Facts` @desc What was done with the property, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 421` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's dishonestly
        OR   f's fraudulently )
   ...  (    f's `removes, conceals, or delivers to any person`
        OR   f's `transfers or causes to be transferred to any person, without adequate consideration` )
   ...  "any property,"
   ...  f's `intending thereby to prevent, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby prevent, the distribution of that property according to law among his creditors or the creditors of any other person`

@export Frame a charge under section 421 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Fraudulent Disposition Facts` @desc The disposition, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 421` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "421" "dishonest or fraudulent removal or concealment of property to prevent distribution among creditors"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 421`'s words)
        (`offence under s 421` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (`dishonestly or fraudulently, recited` f), " ",
                (IF f's `removes, conceals, or delivers to any person` THEN "remove, conceal or deliver to another person" ELSE "transfer or cause to be transferred, without adequate consideration,"),
                " property, to wit, ", f's `the property`,
                ", intending thereby to prevent, or knowing it to be likely that you would thereby prevent, the distribution of that property according to law among your creditors or the creditors of another person")
        (concat (LIST (`missing dishonestly or fraudulently` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `removes, conceals, or delivers to any person` OR f's `transfers or causes to be transferred to any person, without adequate consideration`) "removes, conceals, or delivers to any person, or transfers or causes to be transferred to any person, without adequate consideration, any property"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intending thereby to prevent, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby prevent, the distribution of that property according to law among his creditors or the creditors of any other person`) "intending thereby to prevent, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby prevent, the distribution of that property according to law among creditors")))

§§ `s 422 - dishonestly or fraudulently preventing a debt or demand due to the offender from being made available for his creditors`

-- 422. Whoever dishonestly or fraudulently prevents any debt or demand due to
-- himself or to any other person from being made available according to law for payment
-- of his debts or the debts of such other person, shall be punished with imprisonment for a
-- term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 422
`punishment prescribed by s 422` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "422"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 422 of the Penal Code 1871 (dishonestly or fraudulently preventing a debt or demand from being made available for creditors)
GIVEN f IS A `Fraudulent Disposition Facts` @desc The debt or demand, and what was done with it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 422` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's dishonestly
        OR   f's fraudulently )
   ...  f's `prevents any debt or demand due to himself or to any other person from being made available according to law for payment of his debts or the debts of such other person`

@export Frame a charge under section 422 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Fraudulent Disposition Facts` @desc The debt or demand, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 422` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "422" "dishonestly or fraudulently preventing a debt or demand due to the offender from being made available for his creditors"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 422`'s words)
        (`offence under s 422` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (`dishonestly or fraudulently, recited` f), " prevent a debt or demand, to wit, ", f's `the property`,
                ", from being made available according to law for payment of debts")
        (concat (LIST (`missing dishonestly or fraudulently` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `prevents any debt or demand due to himself or to any other person from being made available according to law for payment of his debts or the debts of such other person`) "prevents any debt or demand from being made available according to law for payment of debts")))

§§ `s 423 - dishonest or fraudulent execution of deed of transfer containing a false statement of consideration`

-- 423. Whoever dishonestly or fraudulently signs, executes, or becomes a party to any
-- deed or instrument which purports to transfer or subject to any charge any property, or
-- any interest therein, and which contains any false statement relating to the consideration
-- for such transfer or charge, or relating to the person or persons for whose use or benefit it
-- is really intended to operate, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
-- extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 423
`punishment prescribed by s 423` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "423"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 423 of the Penal Code 1871 (dishonest or fraudulent execution of deed of transfer containing a false statement of consideration)
GIVEN f IS A `Fraudulent Disposition Facts` @desc The deed, and what it says
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 423` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's dishonestly
        OR   f's fraudulently )
   ...  f's `signs, executes, or becomes a party to any deed or instrument which purports to transfer or subject to any charge any property, or any interest therein`
   ...  ", and"
   ...  f's `which contains any false statement relating to the consideration for such transfer or charge, or relating to the person or persons for whose use or benefit it is really intended to operate`

@export Frame a charge under section 423 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Fraudulent Disposition Facts` @desc The deed, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 423` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "423" "dishonest or fraudulent execution of deed of transfer containing a false statement of consideration"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 423`'s words)
        (`offence under s 423` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (`dishonestly or fraudulently, recited` f), " sign, execute, or become a party to a deed or instrument, to wit, ", f's `the property`,
                ", which purported to transfer or subject to a charge property, and which contained a false statement relating to the consideration for such transfer or charge, or to the person for whose use or benefit it was really intended to operate")
        (concat (LIST (`missing dishonestly or fraudulently` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `signs, executes, or becomes a party to any deed or instrument which purports to transfer or subject to any charge any property, or any interest therein`) "signs, executes, or becomes a party to a deed or instrument which purports to transfer or subject to a charge any property"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `which contains any false statement relating to the consideration for such transfer or charge, or relating to the person or persons for whose use or benefit it is really intended to operate`) "which contains a false statement relating to the consideration, or to the person for whose benefit it is really intended to operate")))

§§ `s 424 - dishonest or fraudulent removal or concealment of property or release of claim`

-- 424. Whoever dishonestly or fraudulently conceals or removes any property of
-- himself or any other person, or dishonestly or fraudulently assists in the concealment or
-- removal thereof, or dishonestly releases any demand or claim to which he is entitled,
-- shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with
-- fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 424
`punishment prescribed by s 424` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "424"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 424 of the Penal Code 1871 (dishonest or fraudulent removal or concealment of property or release of claim)
GIVEN f IS A `Fraudulent Disposition Facts` @desc The property or claim, and what was done with it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 424` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    (    (    f's dishonestly
                  OR   f's fraudulently )
             AND  (    f's `conceals or removes any property of himself or any other person`
                  OR   f's `assists in the concealment or removal thereof` ) )
        OR   (    f's dishonestly
             AND  f's `releases any demand or claim to which he is entitled` ) )

@export Frame a charge under section 424 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Fraudulent Disposition Facts` @desc The property or claim, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 424` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "424" "dishonest or fraudulent removal or concealment of property or release of claim"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 424`'s words)
        (`offence under s 424` f)
        (CONCAT "did ",
                (`joined with` ", and did " (concat (LIST
                    (`included if` ((f's dishonestly OR f's fraudulently) AND f's `conceals or removes any property of himself or any other person`) (CONCAT (`dishonestly or fraudulently, recited` f), " conceal or remove property, to wit, ", f's `the property`)),
                    (`included if` ((f's dishonestly OR f's fraudulently) AND f's `assists in the concealment or removal thereof`) (CONCAT (`dishonestly or fraudulently, recited` f), " assist in the concealment or removal of property, to wit, ", f's `the property`)),
                    (`included if` (f's dishonestly AND f's `releases any demand or claim to which he is entitled`) (CONCAT "dishonestly release a demand or claim to which you were entitled, to wit, ", f's `the property`))))))
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 424` f) "dishonestly or fraudulently conceals or removes property, or assists in its concealment or removal, or dishonestly releases a demand or claim to which he is entitled")

§§ `ss 424A and 424B - fraud by false representation, non-disclosure or abuse of position`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 424A, 424B - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `Fraud by False Representation Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the conduct`         IS A STRING  @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after the limb in the charge - for example "to wit, by representing to one Tan Ah Kow that the said shares were listed on the Singapore Exchange"
    fraudulently          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act fraudulently (s 25)?
    dishonestly           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act dishonestly (s 24)?
    `makes a false representation`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Did the accused make a false representation - a representation, express or implied, as to fact or law (including anyone's state of mind) that is untrue or misleading and that he knows is, or might be, untrue or misleading? A representation submitted to a system or device counts (s 424A(5)). It need not have been material (s 424A(2)).
    `fails to disclose to another person information which he is under a legal duty to disclose`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Did the accused fail to disclose to another person information he was under a legal duty to disclose?
    `abuses a position in which he is expected to safeguard, or not to act against, the financial interests of another person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Did the accused abuse, by act or omission, a position in which he is expected to safeguard, or not to act against, another person's financial interests?
    `directly connected with a written or oral contract for the supply of goods or services`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the representation, non-disclosure or abuse directly connected with a written or oral contract for the supply of goods or services? (s 424A(4): if so, s 424A does not apply)

@export Whether the accused, fraudulently or dishonestly, makes a false representation, fails to disclose, or abuses a position, within section 424A(1) and 424B(1) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Fraud by False Representation Facts` @desc The conduct, and with what intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits fraud by false representation, non-disclosure or abuse of position` f IF
        "(1) A person shall be guilty of an offence if he,"
   ...  (    f's fraudulently
        OR   f's dishonestly )
   ...  (    f's `makes a false representation`
        OR   f's `fails to disclose to another person information which he is under a legal duty to disclose`
        OR   f's `abuses a position in which he is expected to safeguard, or not to act against, the financial interests of another person` )
   ...  "(2) ... whether or not the acts ... were material"

-- 424A.-(1) A person shall be guilty of an offence if he, fraudulently or
-- dishonestly -
--
-- (a) makes a false representation;
--
-- (b) fails to disclose to another person information which he is under a legal
-- duty to disclose; or
--
-- (c) abuses, whether by act or omission, a position which he occupies in which
-- he is expected to safeguard, or not to act against, the financial interests of
-- another person.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (2) A person may be guilty of an offence under subsection (1) whether or not the acts
-- in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) were material.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (3) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be
-- punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, or with fine, or
-- with both.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (4) This section does not apply where the false representation, failure to disclose or
-- abuse of position mentioned in subsection (1) is directly connected with a written or oral
-- contract for the supply of goods or services.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (5) For the purposes of this section and section 424B -
--
-- (a) "representation" means any representation as to fact or law, including a
-- representation as to the state of mind of the person making the
-- representation, or any other person;
--
-- (b) a person makes a false representation if it is untrue or misleading, and that
-- person knows that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading;
--
-- (c) a representation may be express or implied; and
--
-- (d) a representation may be regarded as made if it (or anything implying it) is
-- submitted in any form to any system or device designed to receive, convey
-- or respond to communications (with or without human intervention).
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 424A
`punishment prescribed by s 424A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "424A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 424A of the Penal Code 1871 (fraud not connected with contracts for goods or services)
GIVEN f IS A `Fraud by False Representation Facts` @desc The conduct, and whether it was connected with a contract for goods or services
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 424A` f IF
        `commits fraud by false representation, non-disclosure or abuse of position` f
   ...  "(4) This section does not apply where ... directly connected with a written or oral contract for the supply of goods or services"
   ...  NOT f's `directly connected with a written or oral contract for the supply of goods or services`

-- 424B.-(1) A person shall be guilty of an offence if he, fraudulently or dishonestly
--
-- -
-- (a) makes a false representation;
--
-- (b) fails to disclose to another person information which he is under a legal
-- duty to disclose; or
--
-- (c) abuses, whether by act or omission, a position which he occupies in which
-- he is expected to safeguard, or not to act against, the financial interests of
-- another person.
--
-- (2) A person may be guilty of an offence under subsection (1) whether or not the acts
-- in subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) were material.
--
-- (3) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction be
-- punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, or with fine, or
-- with both.
--
-- (4) This section does not apply to any act mentioned in subsection (1) which would
-- constitute an offence under section 424A.
--
-- [Act 15 of 2019 wef 28/07/2023]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 424B
`punishment prescribed by s 424B` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "424B"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 424B of the Penal Code 1871 (fraud by false representation, non-disclosure or abuse of position)
GIVEN f IS A `Fraud by False Representation Facts` @desc The conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 424B` f IF
        `commits fraud by false representation, non-disclosure or abuse of position` f
   ...  "(4) This section does not apply to any act ... which would constitute an offence under section 424A"
   ...  NOT `offence under s 424A` f

GIVEN f IS A `Fraud by False Representation Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the recital of the fraud` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did ", (`joined with` " and " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's fraudulently) "fraudulently"), (`included if` (f's dishonestly) "dishonestly")))), " ",
           (`joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST
               (`included if` (f's `makes a false representation`) "make a false representation"),
               (`included if` (f's `fails to disclose to another person information which he is under a legal duty to disclose`) "fail to disclose to another person information which you were under a legal duty to disclose"),
               (`included if` (f's `abuses a position in which he is expected to safeguard, or not to act against, the financial interests of another person`) "abuse a position in which you were expected to safeguard, or not to act against, the financial interests of another person")))),
           ", ", f's `the conduct`

GIVEN f IS A `Fraud by False Representation Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of fraud not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's fraudulently OR f's dishonestly) "fraudulently or dishonestly"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `makes a false representation` OR f's `fails to disclose to another person information which he is under a legal duty to disclose` OR f's `abuses a position in which he is expected to safeguard, or not to act against, the financial interests of another person`) "makes a false representation, fails to disclose information he is under a legal duty to disclose, or abuses a position of financial trust"))

@export Frame a charge under section 424A of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Fraud by False Representation Facts` @desc The conduct, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 424A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "424A(1)" "fraud by false representation, non-disclosure or abuse of position not connected with contracts for goods or services"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 424A`'s words)
        (`offence under s 424A` f)
        (`the recital of the fraud` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of fraud not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (NOT f's `directly connected with a written or oral contract for the supply of goods or services`) "not directly connected with a written or oral contract for the supply of goods or services (section 424A(4))")))

@export Frame a charge under section 424B of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Fraud by False Representation Facts` @desc The conduct, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 424B` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "424B(1)" "fraud by false representation, non-disclosure or abuse of position"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 424B`'s words)
        (`offence under s 424B` f)
        (`the recital of the fraud` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of fraud not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (NOT `offence under s 424A` f) "not an act which would constitute an offence under section 424A (section 424B(4))")))
